<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: France, Italy ministers discuss EMU.</title>
<headline>France, Italy ministers discuss EMU.</headline>
<dateline>TRALEE, Ireland 1996-09-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The foreign ministers of France and Italy met privately in the southern Irish town of Tralee on Sunday to discuss a number of issues related to the European Union, including economic and monetary union (EMU), an EC official at the meeting said.</p>
<p>France's Herve de Charette and Italy's Lamberto Dini had spoken on the margins of an informal foreign ministers meeting, agreeing that the Maastricht Treaty's timetable and criteria for EMU must be maintained, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;The treaty, the treaty, the treaty,&quot; the official said, describing the discussion.</p>
<p>He said Dini had not discussed any Italian plans for the lira to rejoin the Exchange Rate Mechanism, but had briefed de Charette on Rome's programme for cutting its budget deficit.</p>
</text>
